/span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Asander was ruler of the Bosporan Kingdom from 47 BCE until about 17 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asano-clan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/asano-clan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asano clan</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Asano clan was a Japanese warrior family that rose through its ties with Toyotomi Hideyoshi, whose wife Nene had been adopted into the family.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asano-nagaakira"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/asano-nagaakira.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asano Nagaakira</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Asano Nagaakira was a Japanese daimyo, son of Asano Nagamasa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asantehene"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/asantehene.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asantehene</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Asantehene is the title of the king of the Asante, the ruler of the Ashanti Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/asantemanhyiamu"><span class="enc-name">Asantemanhyiamu</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Asantemanhyiamu was the national assembly of the Asante kingdom, in which the Asantehene met the paramount chiefs of the member states of the union.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/asar-mahal"><span class="enc-name">Asar Mahal</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Asar Mahal is a palace hall in Bijapur, in present-day Karnataka, built around 1646 by Sultan Muhammad Adil Shah, reputedly as a hall of justice.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ascanius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ascanius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ascanius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ascanius, also called Iulus, is the son of Aeneas in Roman legend.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ascaric"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ascaric.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ascaric</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ascaric was a Frankish king who, with Merogaisus, led raids across the lower Rhine into Roman territory at the start of the 4th century.</span></a></li></ul>
